      "id": 1,
      "text": "Normandy began as Lehmann Ranch in 1878, a small settlement mainly of Mexican ranch workers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/normandy-tx-maverick-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The first post office, named Upson, opened in 1879 and was run by Frank R., before closing in 1901.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/normandy-tx-maverick-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "dropped_surname_no_wiki_source"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1915, Lehmann Ranch served as a U.S. military headquarters during the Mexican Revolution.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/normandy-tx-maverick-county",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Normandy sits 16 miles north‑northwest of Eagle Pass, the Maverick County seat, and 39 miles southeast of Del Rio.",
